# Network Incident Intelligence Platform
**Automated root cause analysis for multi-device network outages**

---

When a network goes down, the last thing you want to do is SSH into 12 devices one by one and manually grep through logs trying to figure out what broke first. This project automates that entire process — it watches all your devices, correlates events across the whole topology, and tells you exactly what failed, when, and why, usually within 60 seconds.

Built for my MS Telecommunications Engineering capstone at University of Maryland, College Park. May 2026.

---

## What it does

A core switch interface goes down at 14:23:01. Two distribution switches lose their OSPF neighbor at 14:23:11. Routes get withdrawn at 14:23:12. 120 users can't reach the application.

Without this system: an engineer SSHs into every device, manually cross-references timestamps, and figures out the cascade after 15-30 minutes.

With this system: the correlation engine detects the interface failure, traces the OSPF and routing chain, identifies the root cause, and generates a plain-English incident report — all in under 60 seconds.

---

## Architecture overview

```
Network Devices (12x Arista vEOS + pfSense)
        |
        |  syslog (UDP 514) + SNMP (every 30s)
        v
Telemetry Collector (Python)
        |
        v
PostgreSQL (time-series event storage)
        |
        v
Correlation Engine (Python + NetworkX)
        |
        +-------> Grafana Dashboards (real-time)
        |
        +-------> Incident Reports (plain English, auto-generated)
```

**Network topology — 4 tiers, 12 devices:**

| Layer | Devices | Protocols |
|-------|---------|-----------|
| Edge | 2x Edge Routers, 2x Firewalls | BGP, VRRP, NAT |
| Core | 2x Core Switches (L3) | OSPF Area 0, HSRP |
| Distribution | 2x Distribution Switches (L3) | VLAN routing, OSPF |
| Access | 2x Access Switches (L2) | 802.1Q trunking |

4 VLANs: Employee, Guest, DMZ, Management

---

## Tech stack

| Component | Tool |
|-----------|------|
| Network devices | Arista vEOS, pfSense |
| Network simulator | GNS3 |
| Telemetry collection | Python (syslog server + PySNMP poller) |
| Database | PostgreSQL |
| Topology modeling | NetworkX |
| Dashboards | Grafana |
| Language | Python 3 |

