## How to run it

### Prerequisites
- GNS3 with Arista vEOS images loaded
- Python 3.9+
- PostgreSQL
- Grafana

### Setup

```bash
git clone https://github.com/YOUR_USERNAME/network-incident-platform
cd network-incident-platform

pip install -r requirements.txt
```

Set up the database:
```bash
psql -U postgres -f docs/schema.sql
```

Start collecting telemetry:
```bash
# terminal 1 — syslog listener
python monitoring/collectors/syslog_collector.py

# terminal 2 — SNMP poller
python monitoring/collectors/snmp_poller.py

# terminal 3 — correlation engine
python monitoring/correlation/incident_engine.py
```

Import the Grafana dashboard from `monitoring/dashboards/grafana-dashboard.json`.

---

## Testing / failure scenarios

I tested 15+ deliberate failure injections:

| Scenario | What I did | What the system caught |
|----------|------------|------------------------|
| Interface failure | Shut down Core-SW-01 Eth2 | Root cause identified, OSPF cascade traced |
| OSPF flap | Repeatedly toggled interface | Flagged as unstable adjacency (5+ flaps / 10 min) |
| HSRP failover | Killed the HSRP active router | Core-SW-02 became gateway in <3 seconds |
| Config error | Misconfigured a VLAN | VLAN 10 clients isolated, caught immediately |
| Link failure | Disconnected core-to-dist cable | Traffic reroute detected, redundant path used |

Target metrics:
- MTTD under 60 seconds ✅
- Root cause accuracy 100% across all scenarios ✅
- Zero false positives ✅

